This port brings xosview to the Mac platform and should run on recent
Darwin/Mach systems.

The Darwin port requires XQuartz.  Its headers and libraries normally live
under /opt/X11.

To build without installing:

  $ cp targets/darwin .config
  $ make

The Darwin target provides load-average, CPU, memory, swap, network, and
disk-I/O meters.

Implemented meters follow the classic Linux display order: load, CPU, memory,
disk, swap, then network.

If an existing X resource database disables the implemented meters, this build
will report that no meters are enabled.  Override those resources for the test:

  $ ./xosview -xrm 'xosview*load: True' -xrm 'xosview*cpu: True' -xrm 'xosview*mem: True' -xrm 'xosview*swap: True' -xrm 'xosview*net: True' -xrm 'xosview*disk: True'
